593250d600ca -> 39c18877e042, tree 3a4a84beb20b343390f5bae64cb166df4d0cfd693baff6309fc13c8060d1c866.

No workflow reference names this leg, so the gitlink and the pin file are the whole of it.

The gitlink at spec, `commit:` and `digests.tree_sha256` in contracts/spec-pin.yaml, and every workflow reference to opensoft/openRepoTools-spec move in ONE commit because `scripts/validate-pins.py` refuses when they disagree — a gitlink advanced alone is red on the next pull request, and on somebody else's change.

Written by openRepoShape's `scripts/bump-leg.py`; the digest is recomputed from the leg's own objects, not adjusted.

Lane: openRepoTools-1
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 contracts/spec-pin.yaml | 4 ++--
 spec                    | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contracts/spec-pin.yaml b/contracts/spec-pin.yaml
index 65f8736..af1d2f7 100644
--- a/contracts/spec-pin.yaml
+++ b/contracts/spec-pin.yaml
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ leg_role: spec
 source_repository: opensoft/openRepoTools-spec
 submodule_path: spec
 
-commit: "593250d600ca291f610671d993c2a6fc36cd690e"
+commit: "39c18877e042e13156849b861d07bc3c92e64db4"
 revision_kind: commit
 
 digest_algorithm: sha256
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ digest_algorithm: sha256
 # <oid>`, so a leg's own pin moving is drift too.
 digest_definition: sorted-ls-tree-r-v1
 digests:
-  tree_sha256: "92da0a8a72f8a9ed3c8827b63e2c39b1734bc1e5418612e2fa41e40b2f148b45"
+  tree_sha256: "3a4a84beb20b343390f5bae64cb166df4d0cfd693baff6309fc13c8060d1c866"
 
